  "articleBody": "Thinking about a new bathroom floor but wondering if you should DIY or call in the experts? There are definitely some clear signs that leaning on a professional is your best bet. If you pull up your old flooring and find that the subfloor is damaged, uneven, or showing signs of water intrusion, that's a big signal. Repairing and leveling a subfloor correctly is crucial, and a pro knows exactly how to handle it. Another cue is if precise waterproofing details are essential for your chosen material, especially around showers and tubs. Getting those seals just right prevents future headaches like leaks and mold. Also, if you're working with tile or other materials that require intricate cutting, a specific layout, or complex patterns, a professional can ensure a flawless finish that you might struggle to achieve on your own. Lastly, if your project involves removing and reinstalling toilets, vanities, or even a tub to get the flooring in, a pro can manage that entire process smoothly. For reliable, quality work that stands the test of time in the Denver area, HH Remodeling LLC is here to help.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}